olivia: Heads up — onboarding RN + the new JS SDK (v1.4.0) is failing for a few partners using Expo dev client. Metro throws a cannot resolve 'crypto' error. @sam any quick ideas?

sam: Hmm. Is that the ESM-only build we shipped? Expo's metro sometimes needs a CJS entry or specific react-native mapping. :grimacing:

olivia: Yeah we defaulted to ESM in the package. Error snippet: 
```
Error: Unable to resolve module `crypto` from `node_modules/@redwood-inference/sdk/dist/index.esm.js`: crypto could not be found within the project.
```

jia: Can you paste your package.json exports/fields? Might be metro using `main` or not honoring `exports`. Also expo snack might prefer CJS.

olivia: Minimal package fields (excerpt):
```
{
  "main": "dist/index.cjs.js",
  "module": "dist/index.esm.js",
  "exports": {
    "import": "dist/index.esm.js",
    "require": "dist/index.cjs.js"
  }
}
```

sam: Two quick options: (1) publish an explicit rn/cjs entry and add a `react-native` field pointing at a CJS build, or (2) teach Metro to alias `crypto` -> `expo-crypto` (or a small shim). For immediate unblock, add a `metro.config.js` with extraNodeModules.

olivia: Trying option 2 first — putting this in metro config unblocked the packager for me: 
```
// metro.config.js
const path = require('path');
module.exports = {
  resolver: {
    extraNodeModules: {
      crypto: path.resolve(__dirname, 'node_modules', 'expo-crypto')
    }
  }
};
```

maria: Nice. FYI TS typing issues too: many RN devs see `Property 'subtle' does not exist on type 'Crypto'` or no global `crypto` in TS. We should document adding "lib": ["ES2020", "DOM"] or include a small `types/rn-crypto.d.ts`.

jia: Also note edge runtimes (bun/deno/worker) have different global shapes. We should track SDK parity: ESM vs CJS vs RN vs Edge. Maybe add `exports` paths like "./react-native": "dist/index.rn.cjs.js" so bundlers pick it.

sam: Agree. I'll draft a change: publish a `dist/index.rn.cjs.js`, add `react-native` field and an `exports` path for `./react-native`. That should keep ESM primary while restoring RN compatibility.

olivia: Another issue popped up: auth retry behavior on mobile — when HMR triggers navigation, inflight requests don't abort because our retry layer doesn't accept an AbortSignal. So you get stuck retries while the app state moves on. Any thoughts?

jia: We should make retry middleware forward an AbortSignal to fetch and also short-circuit retries if aborted. Small patch. I'll sketch it.

maria: I'll add a tiny sample app under `examples/rn-auth-abort` that demonstrates abort-on-unmount and tests 429 -> abort flow. Also update onboarding guide so folks don't hit this blocker.

sam: Plan: (1) quick patch to publish RN CJS entry + `react-native` export, (2) add docs + metro workaround snippet to README, (3) add retry opt-in with AbortSignal support, (4) example app. I'll open PRs and tag you all.

olivia: Perfect — assigning to @sam and @maria. Please cc @jia for the retry changes. Thanks y'all :thumbsup:

